{"id":"bs01","name":"Advertiser Daily Status","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>An ads platform tracks the status of its advertisers every day. You have two tables.</p>\n<p><b>advertisers</b> contains the status of each known advertiser at the end of yesterday:</p>\n<ul><li><code>user_id</code> - the advertiser (unique);</li><li><code>status</code> - one of <code>'NEW'</code>, <code>'EXISTING'</code>, <code>'CHURN'</code>, <code>'RESURRECT'</code>.</li></ul>\n<p><b>daily_pay</b> contains one row per payment made <b>today</b> (an advertiser can pay several times, and only advertisers who paid appear):</p>\n<ul><li><code>user_id</code> - the advertiser;</li><li><code>paid</code> - the amount paid (integer).</li></ul>\n<p>The new status of an advertiser is computed as follows:</p>\n<ul><li>an advertiser that did <b>not</b> pay today becomes <code>'CHURN'</code>;</li><li>an advertiser that paid today and whose status yesterday was <code>'CHURN'</code> becomes <code>'RESURRECT'</code>;</li><li>an advertiser that paid today and is <b>not</b> in <code>advertisers</code> is <code>'NEW'</code>;</li><li>any other advertiser that paid today becomes <code>'EXISTING'</code>.</li></ul>\n<p>Your task is to return the columns <code>user_id</code> and <code>status</code> with the new status of every advertiser (known yesterday or new today), sorted by <code>user_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>advertisers</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>user_id</th><th>status</th></tr><tr><td>bing</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>yahoo</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>alibaba</td><td>EXISTING</td></tr><tr><td>baidu</td><td>EXISTING</td></tr><tr><td>target</td><td>CHURN</td></tr><tr><td>tesla</td><td>CHURN</td></tr><tr><td>morgan</td><td>RESURRECT</td></tr><tr><td>chase</td><td>RESURRECT</td></tr></table></div><p>Table <code>daily_pay</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>user_id</th><th>paid</th></tr><tr><td>yahoo</td><td>45</td></tr><tr><td>alibaba</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>target</td><td>13</td></tr><tr><td>morgan</td><td>600</td></tr><tr><td>fitdata</td><td>25</td></tr><tr><td>fitdata</td><td>5</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>user_id</th><th>status</th></tr><tr><td>alibaba</td><td>EXISTING</td></tr><tr><td>baidu</td><td>CHURN</td></tr><tr><td>bing</td><td>CHURN</td></tr><tr><td>chase</td><td>CHURN</td></tr><tr><td>fitdata</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>morgan</td><td>EXISTING</td></tr><tr><td>target</td><td>RESURRECT</td></tr><tr><td>tesla</td><td>CHURN</td></tr><tr><td>yahoo</td><td>EXISTING</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\nSELECT user_id, status FROM advertisers;\n","hints":["Il faut tous les annonceurs d'hier ET les nouveaux qui ont payé aujourd'hui : FULL OUTER JOIN sur user_id.","Ordre du CASE : d'abord 'pas payé', puis 'statut d'hier = CHURN', puis 'inconnu hier', sinon EXISTING."],"summary_fr":"Mettre à jour le statut de chaque annonceur à partir des paiements du jour : pas payé = CHURN, payé après CHURN = RESURRECT, payé et inconnu hier = NEW, sinon EXISTING.","tags":["FULL JOIN","CASE WHEN","nouveaux utilisateurs"],"minutes":15,"source":"shawlu95/Beyond-LeetCode-SQL (MIT) · Advertiser Status","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"advertisers":{"columns":[["user_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["status","VARCHAR(10)"]],"rows":[["bing","NEW"],["yahoo","NEW"],["alibaba","EXISTING"],["baidu","EXISTING"],["target","CHURN"],["tesla","CHURN"],["morgan","RESURRECT"],["chase","RESURRECT"]]},"daily_pay":{"columns":[["user_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["paid","INT"]],"rows":[["yahoo",45],["alibaba",100],["target",13],["morgan",600],["fitdata",25],["fitdata",5]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["user_id","status"],"rows":[["alibaba","EXISTING"],["baidu","CHURN"],["bing","CHURN"],["chase","CHURN"],["fitdata","NEW"],["morgan","EXISTING"],["target","RESURRECT"],["tesla","CHURN"],["yahoo","EXISTING"]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"advertisers":{"columns":[["user_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["status","VARCHAR(10)"]],"rows":[["a1","CHURN"],["a2","EXISTING"]]},"daily_pay":{"columns":[["user_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["paid","INT"]],"rows":[["a1",10],["a3",7]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["user_id","status"],"rows":[["a1","RESURRECT"],["a2","CHURN"],["a3","NEW"]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}